---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
---
<Base
  title="San Lee · Technical Program Manager, AI Systems"
  description="Technical program manager building reliable AI systems through clear direction, explicit contracts, and evidence-based delivery."
  canonical="https://sanlee.me/"
  ogType="website"
  ogDescription="Technical program manager building reliable AI systems through clear direction, explicit contracts, and evidence-based delivery."
  skipTo="#proof"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
  <!-- 2026-09-09 owner ruling: schema.org jobTitle matches the page title
       and the tagline. The title is Technical Program Manager. The .now
       line stays the true employment line: Senior Product Associate at
       JPMorganChase. This ruling replaces the 2026-09-09 live-walk P3
       that left the two strings apart. Do not edit public/resume.html
       for this change. -->
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "San Lee",
    "url": "https://sanlee.me/",
    "jobTitle": "Technical Program Manager",
    "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JPMorganChase" },
    "description": "Technical program manager building reliable AI systems through clear direction, explicit contracts, and evidence-based delivery.",
    "sameAs": [
      "https://github.com/sanlee-ys",
      "https://www.linkedin.com/in/leesan/"
    ]
  }
  </script>
  <style is:inline>
    /* Method plate (portfolio ADR-004). Page-scoped: the three-part way
       the work is run. Not a second system diagram (that sits below).
       The plate's size, centring, ground, and box stroke moved to
       style.css with the MONOGRAPH figure ladder (ADR-014, landing WO-I1).
       The .fig--plate wrapper and the consolidated .method-plate rule own
       the geometry there, and .mp-box reads --stroke-figure there. This
       island keeps only the ink style.css does not carry. The microtext
       sits at 9px, the ADR-014 floor. No SVG text renders under 9px at a
       320px viewport, and this plate never renders under 1:1. */
    .method-plate .mp-box {
      fill: var(--bg);
      stroke-width: 1;
    }
    .method-plate .mp-title {
      fill: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--font);
      font-size: 10px;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .method-plate .mp-micro {
      fill: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 9px;
    }
    .method-plate .mp-edge {
      fill: none;
      stroke: var(--muted);
      stroke-width: 1.5;
    }
    .method-plate marker path { fill: var(--muted); }

    /* Flagship block (under the router since 2026-09-03). Same rule-and-air
       rhythm as .orientation so the two read as siblings: the index, then the
       flagship entry. No accent fill and no card: the site's austerity is the
       credibility signal, and a banner here would argue against the page's own
       thesis. No opacity on text (ADR-009). */
    .flagship {
      margin: 52px 0 0;
      padding: 18px 0 4px;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--rule-strong);
    }
    .flagship .kicker { margin: 0 0 10px; }
    .flagship .section-title { margin-top: 0; }
    /* Counted figures, set as a record: mono, tabular, not a headline number. */
    .flagship-figure {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      margin: 14px 0 0;
    }
    .flagship-figure span { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

    /* The seat line left the first screen on 2026-09-05, and its .looking
       rule left with it. It read "I want a technical program manager seat on
       an AI systems team." The tagline already states the positioning, and
       the proof band below states the evidence, so the first screen no longer
       asks for a job. The same change named Claude in the lede, in the AI-use
       posture framing (CLAUDE.md). The lede is the owner's copy (OC-1, #269,
       2026-08-30) and no gate freezes it, so a session that changes it adds a
       dated line here.

       ix-s1 and ix-s2 used to sit here. Both blocks moved to work.astro with
       the units they style: the eight-row ledger and the field-note clusters
       (landing WO-E1.1). */

    /* ix-s1 came back on 2026-09-05, because the ledger rows came back. The
       three full decision cards on this page collapsed to three ledger rows,
       and every other rule those rows need is already in style.css: .ledger,
       the footnote counter, the reversal mark, .ledger li a, and
       .ledger li.target. This grid is the one part work.astro keeps
       page-scoped, so it is copied here from work.astro rather than hoisted,
       and the two copies must stay in step. The declarations are byte-equal
       to that page's.

       The .measure scope states what is already true: the ledger sits inside
       section.measure on both pages. The link stays inline in the claim below
       48rem and becomes its own cell only above it, so the phone reader keeps
       the WCAG 2.5.8 inline exception rather than owing three 44px boxes
       (scripts/hit-target.cjs). */
    @media (min-width: 48rem) {
      .measure .ledger li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 10.5rem;
        gap: 4px 24px;
        align-items: start;
      }
      .measure .ledger li .led-to {
        justify-self: end;
        text-align: right;
      }
    }

    /* THE OUT-OF-MEASURE PROSE-LINK RULE LEFT THIS PAGE (OC-F closed).
       Two prose links here sit outside .measure: the capacity-gate link in
       the flagship, and the field-notes pointer between two sections.
       `.measure p a` reaches neither, so both painted in the browser's
       default blue and contrast-check.cjs failed them at 1.97:1 in dark.
       This island carried the fix page-scoped while it waited for an
       integrator. style.css now states it once, for this page and for
       work.html's glossary pointer, which is the same construction. */
  </style>
  </Fragment>

  <header class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>San Lee</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Technical program manager building reliable AI systems.</p>
      <p class="now">Senior Product Associate at JPMorganChase, on collaboration platforms serving 300,000 employees, after seven years in infrastructure and operations.</p>
      <p class="lede">
        I set direction, define the interfaces between teams and systems, and
        gate delivery on evidence. Claude does most of the typing under those
        contracts. The evals and the postmortems on this site are the proof.
      </p>
      <!-- 2026-09-09 owner ruling: one proof result on the 320×568 first
           screen. This list reuses proof cell 01 (same words, same figure,
           same href). It is phone-only. The full band below the nav stays
           the index. Do not invent a new metric here. -->
      <ul class="proof hero-result" aria-label="A result from the record">
        <li data-outcome="reversal"><a href="#decision-grounding"><span class="sr-only">Reversed. </span><span class="proof-claim">Added retrieval grounding, cut it</span> <strong>fixed 0, broke 4</strong></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </header>

  <SiteNav />


  <div class="wrap proof-band" id="proof" tabindex="-1">
    <p class="log-intro band-intro">Calls that shipped, and calls that were reversed.</p>
    <ul class="proof" aria-label="What the record shows">
      <li data-outcome="reversal"><a href="#decision-grounding"><span class="sr-only">Reversed. </span><span class="proof-claim">Added retrieval grounding, cut it</span> <strong>fixed 0, broke 4</strong></a></li>
      <li data-outcome="reversal"><a href="#decision-model"><span class="sr-only">Reversed. </span><span class="proof-claim">Built the premium-model upgrade, declined it</span> <strong>0 rows at 1.97&times; the cost</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="#decision-eval"><span class="proof-claim">Rebuilt the eval, accuracy <em>fell</em></span> <strong>97.3% &rarr; 88.9%</strong></a></li>
      <!-- The one entry that resolves to a page rather than to a card below.
           The band is otherwise an index into the decision log, so this breaks
           that pattern deliberately: the claim is about the instruments rather
           than about one decision, and its proof is six incidents, which is a
           page and not a card. Kept last so the three classifier claims still
           read as a set. -->
      <li class="proof-span"><a href="projects/false-green.html"><span class="proof-claim">Found six of my own checks passing on work that never ran</span> <strong>green in 36s, nothing posted</strong></a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mark-legend"><span class="mark-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span>A doubled rule marks a decision that was reversed.</p>
  </div>

  <main class="wrap" id="work" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="orientation" aria-label="What this record demonstrates">
      <h2 class="kicker">Selected work</h2>
      <p class="orientation-lede">Four views of the work: how I structured the system, measured its decisions, tested a judge, and managed the program. Deeper investigations remain linked throughout the record.</p>
      <ul class="doors-index" aria-label="Four flagship case studies">
        <li><a href="projects/the-system.html"><span class="door-name">The System</span><span class="door-why">Architecture, interfaces, and the integration loop</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="projects/defense-news-classifier.html"><span class="door-name">Classifier</span><span class="door-why">Evaluation, reversals, and evidence-based tradeoffs</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="projects/faithfulness-judge.html"><span class="door-name">Faithfulness Judge</span><span class="door-why">Can an LLM reliably catch a made-up claim?</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="projects/product-and-program.html"><span class="door-name">Product &amp; Program</span><span class="door-why">The work read through a TPM lens</span></a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="diagram-more standalone"><a class="card-link" href="projects/classifier-baseline.html#try-it">Run the classifier demo <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a></p>

      <!-- How the work is run. Open pipeline, no oxide: this is the method,
           not a reversal. ADR-010 N/A. A legacy bare plate takes a div
           wrapper, never a figure (gate law), and a hand-numbered label
           span (ADR-014, PL-3/PL-4). The caption slots stay empty; the
           landing program records the owner-copy ask. -->
      <div class="fig fig--plate">
      <span class="fig-label">Plate 01</span>
      <svg class="method-plate" viewBox="0 0 260 72" role="img"
           aria-label="How the work is run: set the direction, freeze the contracts between the parts, then gate every change on evidence.">
        <title>Direction, then contracts, then an evidence gate.</title>
        <defs>
          <marker id="mp-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5"
                  markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <rect class="mp-box" x="2" y="6" width="76" height="40" rx="2" />
        <text class="mp-title" x="40" y="24" text-anchor="middle">Direction</text>
        <text class="mp-micro" x="40" y="38" text-anchor="middle">set the aim</text>
        <path class="mp-edge" d="M 78 26 L 90 26" marker-end="url(#mp-arrow)" aria-hidden="true" />
        <rect class="mp-box" x="92" y="6" width="76" height="40" rx="2" />
        <text class="mp-title" x="130" y="24" text-anchor="middle">Contracts</text>
        <text class="mp-micro" x="130" y="38" text-anchor="middle">freeze seams</text>
        <path class="mp-edge" d="M 168 26 L 180 26" marker-end="url(#mp-arrow)" aria-hidden="true" />
        <rect class="mp-box" x="182" y="6" width="76" height="40" rx="2" />
        <text class="mp-title" x="220" y="24" text-anchor="middle">Evidence</text>
        <text class="mp-micro" x="220" y="38" text-anchor="middle">gate the merge</text>
        <text class="mp-micro" x="130" y="64" text-anchor="middle">eval gates the merge</text>
      </svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Flagship. The router sits above this block since 2026-09-03, on the
         owner's call after two external reviews (ADR-012, Consequences). Not
         a fifth door: the router holds four views of one system, and this is
         the instrument that measures the capacity that built them. Same
         rule-and-air grammar as .orientation above, so it reads as a promoted
         entry rather than a banner. Every figure here is marked data-tt and
         is gated by scripts/check-telltale-evidence.cjs. No number is typed
         by hand. -->
    <section class="flagship" aria-label="Flagship project">
      <p class="kicker">The instrument</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">telltale</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Five coding-agent CLIs, one brief, five columns &mdash; and gauges that render nothing when nothing was measured.</p>
      <!-- ONE PARAGRAPH AND A LINK, since 2026-09-05 (ADR-012).

           The block held three paragraphs: a lead, an artifact paragraph and
           a method paragraph. The essay lives in full on
           projects/telltale.html, so Home told the case study a second time
           above the fold. The block now states the program, the ruling and
           the instrument in one paragraph, and it sends the reader to the
           writeup for the rest. The block keeps its position above the
           router, which is the order ADR-012 set.

           WHAT LEFT THE BLOCK, AND WHERE IT STILL LIVES. The artifact
           paragraph carried the goldens.zeroVsAbsent figure.
           scripts/check-telltale-evidence.cjs requires a marker on
           projects/telltale.html alone, so Home may carry fewer figures and
           the gate still measures the page it exists for. The method
           paragraph carried the only link on Home to
           projects/product-and-program.html#capacity-gate. The doors list
           below and projects/telltale.html both still reach that page.

           THE COPY STATES NO VENDOR NAME AND NO SPEND CLAIM. No public page
           states either one, and the capacity section reports by evidence
           axis, never by lane and never by name. The section-sub above is
           the one place that counts the seats. -->
      <p>
        I ran a month-long evaluation of the AI coding agents that build this
        record. I wrote the test down before the evidence existed. The
        measurement changed my operating policy. telltale is the instrument
        that reads what five agent CLIs leave on disk.
      </p>
      <p class="flagship-figure">v0.2.0 &middot; <span data-tt="goldens.total">132</span> golden files &middot; <span data-tt="tests.total">1780</span> test functions</p>
      <p class="diagram-more standalone"><a class="card-link" href="projects/telltale.html">The writeup <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a></p>
    </section>

    <h2 class="section-title">The system</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">I wired three services into one loop: an API, an LLM classifier, and a RAG agent.</p>
    <figure class="diagram-wrap">
      <span class="fig-label">Map 02</span>
      <p class="flow-line" aria-label="System data flow, in order">
        Notes API <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        BackgroundTask <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        Classifier <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        Tags <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        Knowledge base <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        KB Agent <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        Grounded answer
      </p>
      <svg class="diagram" id="system-diagram" viewBox="0 0 800 430" role="group" aria-label="Interactive map of the system: notes-api, classifier, and kb-agent. An async BackgroundTasks enrichment loop connects them. Select a component to see what it does and the decision behind it.">
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z"></path>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <g id="diagram-edges"></g>
        <g id="diagram-nodes"></g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="diagram-detail" id="diagram-detail" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Select a component to see what it does and the decision behind it.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="diagram-more standalone"><a class="card-link" href="projects/the-system.html">Read the full writeup <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a></p>

    <section class="measure">
      <h2 class="section-title">The decision log</h2>

      <!-- Three full decision cards stood here until 2026-09-05. They are
           three ledger rows now, in the treatment work.astro already uses, so
           a reader reaches the doors and the proof band in less scrolling.
           ADR-007 records the earlier choice to keep the cards, and it carries
           the dated line for this change.

           THE THREE IDS ARE LOAD-BEARING AND THEY STAY. The proof band above
           links all three by fragment, and scripts/link-check.cjs validates
           every fragment. diagram.js also looks up decision-eval by id on this
           page: that node carries no `away` path, so a lost id would leave the
           classifier node offering no link at all. The id moved from a
           div.decision to an li, and style.css already carries
           `.ledger li.target`, so the highlighter swipe still lands.

           The eight one-row entries moved to work.html#decision-log whole
           (landing WO-E1.1). diagram.js offers two of them at work.html
           through `away` (decision-rightsized and decision-contracts, #269).
           The intro below is the pointer to the full log. -->
      <p class="ledger-intro">Three decisions, one row each. The full log is on Work. <a href="work.html#decision-log">The decision log &rarr;</a></p>
      <ul class="ledger">
        <li id="decision-grounding" data-outcome="reversal"><span class="led-claim"><span class="sr-only">Reversed. </span>I added BM25 retrieval grounding, rebuilt the baseline so both arms ran one prompt, and cut it. It <strong>fixed 0 domain calls and broke 4</strong> across 162 classifications.</span> <span class="led-to"><a href="projects/defense-news-classifier.html#decision-grounding">Classifier &rarr;</a></span></li>
        <li id="decision-model" data-outcome="reversal"><span class="led-claim"><span class="sr-only">Reversed. </span>I built the premium-model upgrade, measured it, and declined it. It moved <strong>0 rows at 1.97&times; the cost</strong> per article, so the default model stays Sonnet.</span> <span class="led-to"><a href="projects/defense-news-classifier.html">Classifier &rarr;</a></span></li>
        <li id="decision-eval"><span class="led-claim">I rebuilt the eval on 54 hand-labeled real snippets, in place of 300 the model wrote itself. Domain accuracy fell <strong>97.3% &rarr; 88.9%</strong>, and the lower number is the trustworthy one.</span> <span class="led-to"><a href="projects/defense-news-classifier.html">Classifier &rarr;</a></span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="measure">
      <h2 class="section-title">Classifier evidence</h2>
      <p>Where the classifier stands now, on 54 hand-labeled real snippets.</p>
      <ul class="stat-strip">
        <li><span class="stat-value" data-metric="category_accuracy">94.4%</span><span class="stat-label">Category</span></li>
        <li><span class="stat-value" data-metric="domain_accuracy">98.1%</span><span class="stat-label">Domain</span></li>
        <li><span class="stat-value" data-metric="region_accuracy">94.4%</span><span class="stat-label">Region</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="stat-note">I score category and region separately. The two figures are equal here by coincidence.</p>
      <!-- The version and the set size sit with the tiles, so a first read
           carries both. `n` is a key of the artifact's gold object, so the
           set size is a checked figure. The version is not under gold, so
           check-published-metrics.cjs has no marker for it; it is plain
           text and it moves by hand on a release. -->
      <p>Classifier v3.2.1 on the <span data-metric="n">54</span>-snippet human-labeled gold set. <a href="projects/defense-news-classifier.html">Full eval &rarr;</a></p>
      <p>The classical baseline lost the case for an LLM. I vendored it here, and it runs in the browser on the same rows. <a href="projects/classifier-baseline.html#try-it">Run it yourself &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <!-- The field-note section moved to work.html#field-notes whole (landing
         WO-E1.1). The twelve titles, the five cluster headings, the ix-s2
         comment, and the ix-s2 CSS travelled byte-exact. This line is the
         pointer that stays behind. It carries the notes-site link the section
         already carried, and it adds no claim. -->
    <p class="muted-line">Field notes on the techniques behind this work sit on the work index. <a href="work.html#field-notes">The field notes &rarr;</a></p>

    <section class="measure about" id="about">
      <h2 class="section-title">About</h2>
      <p>
        For the short version of how I came to this work and how I approach it,
        read <a href="about.html">About &rarr;</a>
      </p>
      <!-- What the way of working produced, stated as things a reader can go
           and check (landing WO-E1.4). Every sentence points at a live
           surface: the reversal legend in the proof band above, the figure
           contract that fails a build on an empty limit slot, and the public
           incident log the colophon already links. Current choice
           (2026-09-04, owner-editable; ADR-011 is Informational): this
           section names no employer internal, no team, and no seat. One
           clause is a gate and stays: no number that no artifact produces
           (scripts/check-published-metrics.cjs). The capacity ruling is
           deliberately not restated, because the flagship above already
           carries it and one page states one claim once. -->
      <p>
        I run this record in the open. A measurement changed what I shipped,
        and a reversed decision carries a doubled rule on the page that
        recorded it. A figure caption states what the figure does not show,
        and the build fails on an empty one. The operating layer keeps its
        <a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/agent-ops">incident log in the open</a>,
        postmortem-first.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is a solo build, so I simulate the program layer. The
        <a href="projects/product-and-program.html">Product &amp; Program</a>
        page states what that means.
      </p>
      <!-- Who built this, named. The lede named AI agents until 2026-09-05
           and names Claude now, so the first screen and this block carry the
           same framing (CLAUDE.md, AI-use posture). This paragraph keeps the
           full framing: direction and bar, the typing, the proof. It sits
           under the solo-build line so "solo" does not read as a claim that
           one person typed it all. -->
      <p>
        I set the direction and the bar. Claude does most of the typing. The
        evals and postmortems are the proof. The
        <a href="colophon.html">colophon</a> states the method in full.
      </p>
      <p>
        A second record sits off this system: a physical lab that makes a
        factory-blank router provision itself.
        <a href="projects/netops-lab.html">Zero-touch provisioning &rarr;</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside the work I hike, take pictures, and live with a Scottish Fold
        named Sango. The rest is on
        <a href="about.html#outside">About</a> and in
        <a href="lab/gallery.html">the gallery</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="frame-strip" aria-label="A few frames from the gallery">
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-pavilion-spring.jpeg" alt="Buyongjeong in the Secret Garden of Changdeokgung (창덕궁 후원)" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-jeju.jpeg" alt="Daepo Jusangjeolli Cliff (주상절리대), Jeju" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-lanterns.jpeg" alt="Yeondeunghoe lotus lanterns (연등)" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-trail.jpeg" alt="A granite overlook on a Korean mountain trail" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="sango">
        <img src="assets/img/sango-boop.jpeg" alt="Sango, a Scottish Fold, asleep" loading="lazy" width="240" height="240" />
        <figcaption>Sango, Chief Nap Officer.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script is:inline src="assets/theme.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="assets/diagram.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="assets/events.js"></script>
</Base>
